<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly unchanged.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The one-week and one-month Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were the only ones that dipped on Monday, while the rest were unchanged, traders said.</p>
<p>PHIBOR continued to reflect the softness in rates due to the high liquidity caused by the imposition of a 20 percent tax on term reverse repos which discouraged banks from reinvesting their money, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect a quiet market today as a result of the New York holiday,&quot; a dealer said.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 Feb 17		  Feb 14</p>
<p>    1 W		9 15/16		 10</p>
<p>    2 W		9 15/16		 9 15/16</p>
<p>    1 M		10  1/16		10  1/8</p>
<p>    2 M		10  1/8		 10  1/8</p>
<p>    3 M		10  3/16		10  3/16</p>
<p>    6 M		10  3/8		 10  3/8</p>
<p>    12M		10  9/16		10  9/16</p>
<p>    VAL		18-Feb		  17-Feb</p>
<p>-- LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
